+# Porto Long Weekend
+
+## Friday, October 16, 2026
+
+- 09:30 — Architecture orientation — Sao Bento Station — begin at the nearby hotel base on a level walk
+- 10:30 — Local market browse — Bolhao Market — take the metro to Bolhao and use its level entrance
+- 12:15 — Lunch with vegetarian option — Bolhao Market — eat in the covered market before continuing by metro
+- 13:45 — [ticketed indoor] Guided architecture visit — Palacio da Bolsa — take the metro to Sao Bento and an STCP bus toward Ribeira
+- 15:30 — Riverside walk with Douro river view — Ribeira promenade — follow the level promenade at an easy pace
+- 18:30 — Dinner with vegetarian option — daTerra Baixa — use the Funicular dos Guindais to avoid the steep uphill walk
+- Rain alternative — replace the Ribeira promenade walk with a covered architecture stop inside Mercado Ferreira Borges.
+
+## Saturday, October 17, 2026
+
+- 09:30 — Azulejo architecture viewing — Igreja do Carmo — take an STCP bus from the Sao Bento area and walk a short level block
+- 10:15 — Garden pause — Cordoaria Garden — walk across the adjacent level square
+- 12:00 — Lunch with vegetarian option — Epoca Porto — take a short, gently paced walk through Cedofeita
+- 13:45 — [ticketed indoor] Architecture tour — Casa da Musica — ride the metro via Trindade to Casa da Musica
+- 15:30 — Neighborhood architecture walk — Rotunda da Boavista — use the level crossings beside the metro station
+- 16:30 — Gardens and Douro river view — Palacio de Cristal Gardens — take an STCP bus and stay on the level main paths
+- 18:45 — Dinner with vegetarian option — Em Carne Viva — ride an STCP bus back toward Boavista
+- Rain alternative — replace Palacio de Cristal Gardens with unhurried browsing inside the free Bombarda galleries.
+
+## Sunday, October 18, 2026
+
+- 09:30 — Metro ride across the Douro — Jardim do Morro — take Metro Line D from Sao Bento to the viewpoint station
+- 10:00 — Porto skyline and river view — Jardim do Morro — use the level terrace beside the metro exit
+- 10:45 — Monastery architecture viewing — Mosteiro da Serra do Pilar terrace — follow the short upper approach and avoid climbing from the riverfront
+- 12:15 — Lunch with vegetarian option — Root & Vine — walk gently through the clustered WOW district
+- 13:45 — [ticketed indoor] Cork museum visit — Planet Cork at WOW — use the nearby indoor entrance within the same district
+- 15:30 — Level Douro promenade — Gaia riverfront — descend by local public transit and stroll without backtracking
+- 16:30 — Craft market browse — Cais de Gaia craft market — continue along the same level riverfront
+- 18:15 — Dinner with vegetarian option — Root & Vine — return by local public transit to the WOW district
+- Rain alternative — replace the Gaia riverfront and craft market browse with the sheltered public area at WOW covered courtyard.
+
+## Practical Notes
+
+- Travelers: two adults sharing a relaxed three-day plan.
+- Food: one traveler is vegetarian and the other has no dietary restriction, so every lunch and dinner includes a vegetarian option.
+- Mobility: start each day at 09:30 or later and finish by 20:30, avoid steep uphill walks, keep the pace easy, minimize backtracking, and cluster each day by nearby neighborhoods.
+- Transport: use walking and public transit only, favoring metro, STCP bus, and funicular connections.
